// ============================================================================
// DIVISION EAP TARGETING EMAIL: BUYER ROLL-UP  (HubSpot workflow custom code, Node 24)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT THIS CODE DOES (big picture)
//
// Runs once per contact inside a CONTACT-based workflow, right before the
// "Send email" step. For that contact it:
//
//   1. Finds the Company (or Companies) the contact belongs to.
//   2. Finds every Division on that Company that has eligible AP.
//   3. Finds which of those Divisions the contact is ALSO associated to.
//   4. Rolls everything up by UNIQUE BUYER (buyer_division_uuid) so each buyer
//      appears once, no matter how many Divisions it has.
//   5. Marks each buyer as:
//        ASSOCIATED - the contact is tied to at least one of that buyer's
//                     Divisions  -> shown as a normal invoice-alert row.
//        MISSING    - the Company has eligible Divisions for that buyer but
//                     the contact is tied to none of them -> shown in the
//                     "Did you know <company> has multiple customers..." block.
//   6. Hands back ready-to-drop-in HTML blocks plus a few small values
//      (outputFields) that the workflow/email uses, same pattern as the
//      Actionable Offer V3 workflow.
//
// If there is nothing to show, it returns safe empty values and message_type
// = "none" so the workflow can skip the send instead of emailing a blank.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SETUP IN THE WORKFLOW
//   Secret:  EAP_SERVICE_KEY_TOKEN  (dedicated service key, NOT the shared AO token)
//     Scopes: crm.objects.contacts.read, crm.objects.companies.read,
//             crm.objects.custom.read (covers the Divisions object + associations)
//   Input fields:  contact_id             <-  Contact property "Record ID" (hs_object_id)
//                  contact_email_language <-  Contact property hubspot_email_language
//                  contact_registration_status <-  Contact property
//                                          c2fo_user_registration_status__c
//                                          ("2" = registered -> button opens the app login;
//                                           anything else -> buyer microsite)
//   Languages: English, Spanish, French, German, Italian, Portuguese, Simplified
//   Chinese (same set as the Invoice Alert email). Drives table headers, the
//   "Did you know..." block, and number/date/currency formatting.
//   Output fields (all type STRING) -- add these names exactly in the action:
//     message_type, company_name, associated_buyer_count, missing_buyer_count,
//     associated_invoice_count, associated_buyers_table, missing_buyers_block,
//     missing_buyers_text, expand_network_url, subject_line, headline_text,
//     intro_text, closing_text, footnote_text, button_label,
//     top_buyer_permalink, top_buyer_name, top_buyer_microsite_url,
//     button_url   (NEW: 19 total; the email button uses this, see below)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// OPEN DECISIONS (settings below, no rebuild needed to change them)
//   MIXED_BUYER_MODE   - what to do when a buyer has some Divisions the contact
//                        is tied to and some it isn't. See comment on the setting.
//   EXCLUDED_BUYER_UUIDS - buyers to suppress. Fill from the buyer review
//                        workbook (rows marked Suppress = Y). Empty = none.
// ============================================================================

